resource  aUpdated irregularly  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier1 aBegan in 2013.  a"Please Note: These guidelines are updated frequently. Superseded text is replaced by new text or deleted"--At head of Introduction.  aThe content is made available by the U.S. Government Publishing Office in accordance with Title 44 of the US Code.  aDigital collection: Federal Depository Library Program Web Archive.  a"The U.S. Government Publishing Office (GPO) Cataloging Guidelines were developed by staff in the Library Services and Content Management (LSCM), Bibliographic Control and Metadata Section with assistance from staff throughout LSCM. These guidelines are intended to provide specific examples and practices that are unique to the cataloging and creation of various types of metadata for U.S. Government information published by all three branches of the Federal Government and in all formats. These guidelines are used by staff at GPO but are also intended for use by staff in Federal depository libraries and library staff in other institutions who handle, process, or use U.S. Government information"--Introduction.  aDescription based on: archived web page captured Apr 20, 2017 (page last updated November 14 2016); title from title screen (viewed Aug. 18, 2017). 0aCataloging of government publicationszUnited StatesvHandbooks, manuals, etc.10aUnited States.bGovernment Publishing Office.bLibrary Technical ServicesvHandbooks, manuals, etc.20aFederal Depository Library ProgramvHandbooks, manuals, etc. 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf2014026109 7aHandbooks and manuals.2lcgft0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf20140261092 aFederal Depository Library Program,ecollector.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n868626271 aUnited States.bGovernment Publishing Office,edistributor.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no20150025030 tFederal D