  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier0 aauditorybclosedcaptions2sapdv  adigital2rdatr  avideo file2rdaft  a"Premiered: May 09, 2025"--Army University Press website.  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aProduced by Randy G. Masten, PhD, Chris Carey, PhD ; executive producers, LTG Milford Beagle, Jr., BG David Foley, COL Todd Schmidt, PhD, LTC Marc Cleveland, Don Wright, PhD ; lead editor, Sara Carlsen ; associate producer, Sara Carlsen ; camera operators, Sara Carlsen, Nick Schale ; assistant editor, Andrew Cornwell ; unit production manager, Nick Schale ; archival research, sound editor, title design, and 3D animation, Sara Carlsen.0 aFeaturing: LTC Marc Cleveland, 1SG Daniel Fields, PFC Rylan Parsons, Leah Cleveland.  a"Filmed in frigid upstate New York at Fort Drum and the majestic Colorado Rockies near Camp Hale, The High Ground follows soldiers of the 10th Mountain Division (LI) as they attempt to reconnect with their alpine roots by completing a mountain marathon eighty years in the making. The film features footage of Army soldiers skiing, snowshoeing, climbing, rappelling, and glissading during 10th Mountain Division events including the D-Series, the Hale to Vail Traverse, and Legacy Days. Army University Films and the 10th MD partnered with the Denver Public Library Special Collections and Archives, History Colorado, the National Ski Patrol (NSP), Vail Resorts, the National Outdoor Leadership School (NOLS), 10th Special Forces Group (Airborne), and the Colorado Army National Guard to create this documentary"--Army University Press website.1 aClosed captioning available in English  aDescription based on online resource; title from landing page (AUP, viewed April 21, 2026).10aUnited States.bArmy.bMountain Division, 10thxHistory.